          ":question/id": "04f20251-29bc-55e7-a2e7-4fe850dcd999",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-130924",
          ":question/problem": "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+8y &=4 \\\\ -3x+12y &=6.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 8 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 10 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 8 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 12 & 6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 12 & 6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-4y &=-2 \\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-4y=-2.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=4y-2,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=4y-2 \\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4y-2 \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"
